rem A typo in a case label used to WEDGE THE PROMPT PERMANENTLY. The compiler
rem answers "expected 'case' or 'endselect'" both when the input ran out and when
rem a wrong token turned up where the label belonged, and the REPL read the
rem message alone -- so it waited for a line that could never come, swallowing
rem everything typed after the mistake, for as long as the session lasted.
rem
rem The compiler now records whether the failure happened AT the end of input,
rem and the prompt waits only then. The error below is reported at once and the
rem session carries on; the error text is on stderr and not in this transcript.
kept = 7
select case 2
csae 2
println "the session came back: " + str$(kept)
select case 3
case 3
println "and a correct select still waits and runs"
endselect
